+### Live provider check (real USDA + Open Food Facts)
+
+All automated suites below use mocked `fetch` or the local stub. To verify the **real** providers, run the app on a
+machine with internet access, using your real `.env` (with `FDC_API_KEY` set and no `FDC_BASE_URL`/`OFF_BASE_URL`
+overrides) and a **test database** (a `DATABASE_URL` whose database name contains `test`, e.g. `fitdb_test`). Then, in a
+second terminal with the same `.env`, run:
+
+```bash
+node --env-file=.env scripts/live-provider-check.cjs        # BASE_URL defaults to http://localhost:3000
+```
+
+- It goes through the app's own API (the existing server-side provider clients). It never prints the key, and only uses it to
+  confirm no response contains it.
+- It refuses to run (exit 4, nothing written) unless all of these hold:
+  - `BASE_URL` is local.
+  - The database name contains `test` (override with `LIVE_CHECK_ALLOW_DATABASE=<name>`).
+  - The **running server's own database** is proven to be that same database. The script compares the server's
+    `GET /api/health/db-identity` fingerprint (an opaque hash) with its own, before any sign-up or other write.
+  - That database carries the explicit **test-database marker**, as reported by the server through the same endpoint. A
+    database name containing `test` isn't enough. Mark a *dedicated* test database once, deliberately:
+    ```bash
+    node --env-file=<test env> scripts/mark-test-database.cjs --confirm fitdb_test
+    ```
+    The marker is a PostgreSQL comment, `fitworkoutfoodtracker:test-database:v1:<database name>`. Migrations never set it.
+
+  The endpoint is on under `npm run dev`. For a production build (`npm start`), set `EXPOSE_DB_IDENTITY=1` on the server.
+- The throwaway `live-check-*@example.test` users it creates are deleted at the end, including after failures and Ctrl+C.
+  Their entries, targets and custom foods are removed by cascade.
+- It reports **LIVE VERIFICATION: PASSED** (exit 0) only with real-provider evidence: no stub overrides, food origins
+  recorded as `api.nal.usda.gov` / `world.openfoodfacts.org`, and realistic result counts. It also needs 0 failed and
+  0 not run. Otherwise it reports NOT LIVE (exit 3) or INCOMPLETE OR FAILED (exit 1).
+- It writes `live-provider-report.json` (git-ignored, no secrets).
 
